---
import { WIN_URL, MSI_URL, MAC_URL, REPO_URL } from '../release';
---
<section id="install" class="wrap">
  <div class="rv">
    <p class="eyebrow">INSTALL</p>
    <h2 class="h2 title">Download, run, done. Updates happen inside the app.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="rv grid" style="--col:340px">
    <div class="card pad">
      <h3>Windows</h3>
      <p>Windows is the primary target. WebView2 is preinstalled on Windows 11.</p>
      <p>Builds are not code-signed, so SmartScreen may ask you to confirm the first run.</p>
      <div class="acts">
        <a class="btn btn-p btn-md" href={WIN_URL}>Download .exe</a>
        <a class="btn btn-s btn-md" href={MSI_URL}>.msi</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card pad">
      <h3>macOS</h3>
      <p>A universal build that runs on Apple silicon and Intel.</p>
      <p>The app is not notarized, so macOS blocks the first launch, once. Try to open it, then go to System Settings, Privacy &amp; Security, scroll to Security and click Open Anyway.</p>
      <p>On macOS 15 and later, right-click and Open no longer works. In a terminal, <code>xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/EmberTerm.app</code> clears the block too.</p>
      <div class="acts">
        <a class="btn btn-p btn-md" href={MAC_URL}>Download .dmg</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card pad src">
      <h3>From source</h3>
      <p>Needs Rust 1.85+, Node.js 22+ and pnpm 9+.</p>
      <pre>git clone https://github.com/emberterm/emberterm
cd emberterm
pnpm install
pnpm dev</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="rv policy" id="code-signing-policy">
    <h3>Code signing policy</h3>
    <p>Windows installers are not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen may warn on first run. EmberTerm is applying for free code signing provided by SignPath.io, certificate by SignPath Foundation. If the application is accepted, this policy applies to the Windows installers:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Free code signing provided by <a href="https://signpath.io">SignPath.io</a>, certificate by <a href="https://signpath.org">SignPath Foundation</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Authors, reviewers and approvers:</b> the EmberTerm maintainers (<a href="https://github.com/orgs/emberterm/people?query=role%3Aowner">owners</a>).</li>
      <li><b>What is signed:</b> only installers built by the <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/.github/workflows/release.yml`}>Release workflow</a> from a version tag, and only after a maintainer approves the signing request for that release.</li>
      <li><b>Privacy:</b> EmberTerm has no telemetry and sends nothing about you. Check for updates asks GitHub for the latest release and its notes; links open only when you click them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>macOS builds are ad-hoc signed and not notarized, because notarization needs a paid Apple Developer Program membership.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .title { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .card { border-color: var(--border); border-radius: 14px; }
  .pad { padding: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; min-width: 0; }
  .src { background: var(--bg-deep); }
  h3 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  p { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .acts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: auto; padding-top: 8px; }
  code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; color: var(--text); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .policy { margin-top: 48px; max-width: 760px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .policy h3 { font-size: 20px; }
  .policy ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .policy b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .policy a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  pre { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; overflow-x: auto; }
</style>
